apiv2-retry-safety.json is an excerpt of the server's API v2 contract: the
method, path template and x-silo-retry-safety class of every annotated
operation, sorted by path then method. Do not hand-edit it. Regenerate it from
the server repository, never from a working tree:

  git -C "$SILO_SERVER_REPO" show 84ed9e596:contracts/api/v2/openapi.json \
    | jq -S '[.paths | to_entries[] | .key as $p | .value | to_entries[]
        | select(.value | type == "object" and has("x-silo-retry-safety"))
        | {method: (.key | ascii_upcase), path: $p, retry_safety: .value["x-silo-retry-safety"]}]
        | sort_by(.path, .method)' \
    > iosApp/Tests/Fixtures/APIv2RetrySafety/apiv2-retry-safety.json

The commit must match the one in Fixtures/APIv2/SOURCE. Whenever
scripts/sync-apiv2-fixtures.sh moves the API v2 fixtures to a new server
commit, regenerate this excerpt at the same commit and update the commit
above. APIv2RetrySafetyTests then checks APIv2MutationCatalog
(iosApp/iosApp/Networking/APIv2/APIv2RetrySafety.swift) against it; update the
catalog in the same change when it fails.

The excerpt lives outside Fixtures/APIv2 because the sync script deletes any
JSON there that it does not list.
